A1. This might be that future shadow that you should avoid. ~ SILHOUETTE
A9. A sign that will always lure a Scotchman. ~ FREE
A13. Someone is always trying to string this one. ~ PEARL
A14. We will have to make allowances for this one. ~ RATIONS
A16. Belonging to. ~ OF
A18. This used to spout a good deal but no one has heard from it lately. ~ ETNA
A19. This one's life is intense and he always prefers a camel. ~ ARAB
A20. This used to stand for tea-parties but now it is talking pictures. ~ TP
A21. They even do this to time in Chicago. ~ KILL
A23. This is even more silent than Cal. ~ SPHINX
A25. Women do this for a peeling effect when they know their onions. ~ CRY
A26. Any Yale man will tell you this helps make eligibility. ~ ELI
A27. These never make dutiful daughters. ~ SONS
A28. The farmer is usually baek of this. ~ HOE
A29. You might make this when you are not sure of your word. ~ STAB
A31. These always look slick. ~ EELS
A32. You will have to go to the ends of the earth for this kind of a thing. ~ POLAR
A34. This is what the winner always gets. ~ THRILL
A36. Here is some food for thought—in Chicago this was skinned, beaten and even had its eyes dug out. ~ POTATO
A37. This kind of a girl has a calling in just plugging along at a number of things. ~ TELEPHONE
A38. You will find the berries in these. ~ CRATES
A41. This is good for the toothache. ~ RELIEF
A44. High fliers that have reached the end of their string. ~ KITES
A45. This one started a lot of trouble in one of those lowdown joints. ~ GOUT
A47. They never serve peaches or pairs at this kind of a dinner. ~ STAG
A48. This is what makes one think he is a German. ~ VON
A49. It won't be long now. ~ SOON
A50. Alphabetically speaking this is what they do when Greek meets Greek. ~ ETA
A51. The end of the little pig that went to market. ~ HAM
A52. Before the company had gone did you ever do this to yawn? ~ STIFLE
A54. A Hebrew measure. ~ OMER
A55. You all know this fellow—he needs no introduction. ~ AL
A56. This is deery himself. ~ PART
A57. Don't keep this up your sleeve this summer (plur.). ~ ARMS
A59. The motorcycle cops are on to this (abbr.). ~ RD
A60. This is what a certain Benedict was. ~ TRAITOR
A62. A favorite pitcher of the Yankees. ~ CREAM
A64. These are usually good lookers. ~ EYES
A65. This one has a hard time in getting by. ~ PEDESTRIAN

D1. This has an upstanding reputation in the community and is an inveterate smoker. ~ SMOKESTACK
D2. The lonesome pine initials. ~ LP
D3. This might be Cuban or it might be French. Women fall for the French. ~ HEEL
D4. The kind of a meal they had for breakfast. ~ OAT
D5. Ash receivers. ~ URNS
D6. This is what time will do. ~ ELAPSE
D7. Many of these are limited. For express purposes. ~ TRAINS
D8. What a woman does to every cent she gets. ~ EARNS
D9. A little thing that comes from a pack of lies. ~ FIB
D10. The kind of a man Caesar was (abbr.). ~ RO
D11. To beseech. ~ ENTREAT
D12. What poets do when they catch sight of the statue of liberty. ~ ESPY
D15. A duty to your country. ~ TAX
D17. Dirt. ~ FILTH
D22. Believe it or not this one lies in a vertical position. ~ LIAR
D24. The only safe kind of socks to wear in Chicago. ~ HOLEPROOF
D25. A half portion of a popular drink. ~ COLA
D28. This is where motorists often stop (plur.). ~ HOTELS
D30. What Fido got for fighting. ~ BITTEN
D31. Old-fashioned measures. ~ ELLS
D32. Johnny-cake. ~ PONE
D33. A place where amusements come high. ~ ROOFGARDEN
D35. The dregs of crossword puzzles. ~ LEES
D36. A good place for a workman to get aboard. ~ PORT
D39. This was between the winners and the losers. ~ RIVALRY
D40. You don't find them much smaller than this. ~ ATOM
D42. A piece of news for you. ~ ITEM
D43. What a little moth is. ~ EATER
D45. Don't let this get you in the neck. ~ GOITRE
D46. To loosen up. ~ UNLACE
D49. This made them keen. ~ STROP
D51. What people do to get up in the morning. ~ HATE
D52. What dad did before he got on his feet. ~ SAT
D53. What every human being does sometime. ~ ERRS
D54. A ridge that sometimes gets in puzzles. ~ OSAR
D56. The kind of presence a woman likes. ~ PIS
D58. What they did at the naval conference. ~ MET
D61. African elephants as they stand in a puzzle. ~ AE
D63. Although this is musical it is partly mistaken. ~ MI


